# R2826 — a GOLDEN is bytes a test compares against, not prose, so its line
# endings are part of its content and must survive every checkout.
#
# Without a declaration, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf, the runner default)
# rewrites LF to CRLF, and the stats-registry golden's reader, which splits on
# "===== END\n", found no scenario end: hosted `portability (windows-latest)`
# failed `wz-session-core` on run 35951199951 while every Linux lane passed.
# Declaring the kind rather than the one file is what covers the next golden.
*.golden text eol=lf
